{
  "id": 20,
  "name": "return_aware_spread_deflection",
  "intent": "Add a (1-p)-modulated penalty proportional to the spread of the candidate's distances to all unvisited cities. This deflects high-spread candidates (likely cluster boundaries or isolated directions) to later in the tour, complementing the parent's hub penalty (which targets low nearest_remaining) and cluster density term. The penalty vanishes as p→1, preserving the parent's strong late-tour return-aware closure. The goal is to reduce early long jumps and improve structural coherence, especially in clustered instances, without altering the linear return-aware and regret backbone.",
  "tags": [
    "return_aware",
    "lookahead"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    d = f[\"distance\"]\n    r = f[\"return_distance\"]\n    nr = f[\"nearest_remaining\"]\n    g = f[\"regret\"]\n    p = f[\"progress\"]\n    cd = f[\"cluster_density\"]\n    sp = f[\"spread\"]\n    return -d + (0.15 + 0.40 * p) * r + (0.35 - 0.20 * p) * g + 0.06 * (1 - p) * cd - 0.08 * (1 - p) * nr - 0.05 * (1 - p) * sp",
